editor.setting.channels = Channels
editor.setting.channels.help = How this node treats the channels of an interleaved signal: R, G, B of video, L, R of stereo.
editor.setting.channels.together = Together
editor.setting.channels.together.help = Runs R, G, B, R, G, B… (or L, R, L, R…) through the node as one
  stream. Channels bleed into each other, as in a low pass or a modulated delay.
editor.setting.channels.separate = Separate
editor.setting.channels.separate.help = Runs each channel through its own copy of the node. The same as
  Split Channels → the node once per channel → Combine Channels.

